omorrow\nAll I need is here today\n\n[Bridge]\nMaybe time will keep on turning\nMaybe everything will change\nBut tonight the music holds us\nLike a fire inside the rain\n\n[Chorus]\nStay with me until the morning\nLet the city fade away\nWe don't need to chase tomorrow\nAll I need is here today",360,0,"yue2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors","sheetsage2_bf16.safetensors",0,false,"melody","keep","nearest_key_safe","dpm_2","sgm_uniform",120,"none","none",1,1],"widgets_values_named":{"value":"English, soulful jazz-pop, expressive male vocal, relaxed 88 BPM, Rhodes piano, upright bass, brushed drums, warm saxophone, subtle strings, intimate late-night atmosphere, rich and organic live-band production","value_1":"[Verse]\nStreetlights shimmer on the pavement\nMidnight breathing soft and slow\nEvery corner holds a memory\nOf the places we used to know\n\n[Chorus]\nStay with me until the morning\nLet the city fade away\nWe don't need to chase tomorrow\nAll I need is here today\n\n[Verse]\nOld café beneath the neon\nRain is falling on the glass\nEvery song becomes a story\nEvery moment moves too fast\n\n[Chorus]\nStay with me until the morning\nLet the city fade away\nWe don't need to chase tomorrow\nAll I need is here today\n\n[Bridge]\nMaybe time will keep on turning\nMaybe everything will change\nBut tonight the music holds us\nLike a fire inside the rain\n\n[Chorus]\nStay with me until the morning\nLet the city fade away\nWe don't need to chase tomorrow\nAll I need is here today","max_duration":360,"seed":0,"ckpt_name":"yue2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors","audio_encoder_name":"sheetsage2_bf16.safetensors","memory_budget_gib":0,"offload_ar":false,"mode":"melody","tempo_mode":"keep","mode_1":"nearest_key_safe","sampler_name":"dpm_2","scheduler":"sgm_uniform","bpm":120,"ar_lora":"none","adapter":"none","ar_strength":1,"nar_strength":1}},{"id":45,"type":"LoadAudio","pos":[800,-260],"size":[590,140],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"audio","name":"audio","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"audio"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"audioUI","name":"audioUI","type":"AUDIO_UI","widget":{"name":"audioUI"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"choose file to upload","name":"upload","type":"AUDIOUPLOAD","widget":{"name":"upload"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"AUDIO","name":"AUDIO","type":"AUDIO","links":[97]}],"properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.37.0","Node name for S&R":"LoadAudio","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["yue2_reference_song.flac",null],"widgets_values_named":{"audio":"yue2_reference_song.flac","upload":null}},{"id":46,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[220,-260],"size":[550,1906.640625],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{"ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["# YuE2: Music Cover\n\nCreate a new version of an existing song with YuE2.\n\nThis workflow uses **SheetSage2** to transcribe the melody from the reference audio into an editable ABC score, then uses YuE2 to regenerate the song with a new **Style** and **Lyrics**.\n\n## Input Asset\n\n- [yue2_reference_song.flac](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/yue2_reference_song.flac)\n\n## Model Links\n\n**checkpoints**\n\n- [yue2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/YuE2/resolve/main/checkpoints/yue2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n\n**audio_encoders**\n\n- [sheetsage2_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/YuE2/resolve/main/audio_encoders/sheetsage2_bf16.safetensors)\n\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n├── 📂 models/\n│   ├── 📂 checkpoints/\n│   │   └── yue2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors\n│   └── 📂 audio_encoders/\n│       └── sheetsage2_bf16.safetensors\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\n[Subgraph](https://docs.comfy.org/interface/features/subgraph)\n\n1. Load a reference song in **Audio**.\n2. Describe the new musical direction in **Style**.\n3. Enter the lyrics you want to sing in **Lyrics**.\n4. Run the workflow to generate a new cover version.\n\nThe reference audio provides the melody, while YuE2 creates a new performance and arrangement based on your Style and Lyrics.\n\n## Writing the Style\n\nDescribe the target musical style clearly.\n\nUseful elements include:\n\n- **Genre:** jazz, pop, rock, folk, electronic\n- **Vocals:** warm male vocal, expressive female vocal, soft vocals\n- **Language:** English, Chinese, Japanese, etc.\n- **Tempo:** 90 BPM, slow, upbeat\n- **Instruments:** piano, guitar, bass, drums, strings, synths\n- **Mood:** intimate, energetic, nostalgic, cinematic\n\nExample:\n\n> English, soulful jazz-pop, expressive male vocal, relaxed 88 BPM, Rhodes piano, upright bass, brushed drums, warm saxophone, intimate late-night atmosphere\n\n## Writing Lyrics\n\nUse section tags such as:\n\n    [Verse]\n    Streetlights shimmer on the pavement\n    Midnight breathing soft and slow\n\n    [Chorus]\n    Stay with me until the morning\n    Let the city fade away\n\nYou can use:\n\n`[Verse]` · `[Chorus]` · `[Bridge]` · `[Outro]`\n\nFor better melody matching, keep the new lyrics reasonably close to the original phrasing and syllable count.\n\n## How the Cover Works\n\nThe workflow does not directly use the reference audio as YuE2 conditioning.\n\nInstead:\n\n    Reference Audio\n        ↓\n    SheetSage2\n        ↓\n    Melody ABC\n        ↓\n    YuE2 + Style + Lyrics\n        ↓\n    New Cover Audio\n\nSheetSage2 converts the source recording into a symbolic melody representation. YuE2 then uses that melody as the musical plan for the new cover.\n\n## Tips\n\n- Keep **Style** focused on the target sound, not the original sound.\n- Use **melody-only** planning for most cover tasks.\n- Changing the Style can create a very different arrangement while preserving the melody.\n- Lyrics can be changed, but similar phrasing and syllable counts usually fit the original melody better.\n- For a simple style-transfer test, keep the original lyrics and only change the Style.\n- For a stronger reinterpretation, change both the Style and Lyrics.\n\n## Learn More\n\n- [YuE2 Cover Guide](https://github.com/multimodal-art-projection/YuE/blob/main/docs/covers.md)\n- [YuE2 Music Skill](https://github.com/multimodal-art-projection/YuE/blob/main/skills/yue2-music/SKILL.md)\n- [Generation & Covers Reference](https://github.com/multimodal-art-projection/YuE/blob/main/skills/yue2-music/references/generation-and-covers.md)\n\n## Report Issue\n\nNote: Please update ComfyUI first ([guide](https://docs.comfy.org/installation/update_comfyui)) and prepare required models. Desktop/Cloud updates follow stable releases, so some nightly-supported models may not be available yet.\n\n- Cannot run / runtime errors: [ComfyUI/issues](https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI/issues)\n- UI / frontend issues: [ComfyUI_frontend/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI_frontend/issues)\n- Workflow issues: [workflow_templates/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/issues)\n"],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"# YuE2: Music Cover\n\nCreate a new version of an existing song with YuE2.\n\nThis workflow uses **SheetSage2** to transcribe the melody from the reference audio into an editable ABC score, then uses YuE2 to regenerate the song with a new **Style** and **Lyrics**.\n\n## Input Asset\n\n- [yue2_reference_song.flac](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/yue2_reference_song.flac)\n\n## Model Links\n\n**checkpoints**\n\n- [yue2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/YuE2/resolve/main/checkpoints/yue2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n\n**audio_encoders**\n\n- [sheetsage2_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/YuE2/resolve/main/audio_encoders/sheetsage2_bf16.safetensors)\n\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n├── 📂 models/\n│   ├── 📂 checkpoints/\n│   │   └── yue2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors\n│   └── 📂 audio_encoders/\n│       └── sheetsage2_bf16.safetensors\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\n[Subgraph](https://docs.comfy.org/interface/features/subgraph)\n\n1. Load a reference song in **Audio**.\n2. Describe the new musical direction in **Style**.\n3. Enter the lyrics you want to sing in **Lyrics**.\n4. Run the workflow to generate a new cover version.\n\nThe reference audio provides the melody, while YuE2 creates a new performance and arrangement based on your Style and Lyrics.\n\n## Writing the Style\n\nDescribe the target musical style clearly.\n\nUseful elements include:\n\n- **Genre:** jazz, pop, rock, folk, electronic\n- **Vocals:** warm male vocal, expressive female vocal, soft vocals\n- **Language:** English, Chinese, Japanese, etc.\n- **Tempo:** 90 BPM, slow, upbeat\n- **Instruments:** piano, guitar, bass, drums, strings, synths\n- **Mood:** intimate, energetic, nostalgic, cinematic\n\nExample:\n\n> English, soulful jazz-pop, expressive male vocal, relaxed 88 BPM, Rhodes piano, upright bass, brushed drums, warm saxophone, intimate late-night atmosphere\n\n## Writing Lyrics\n\nUse section tags such as:\n\n    [Verse]\n    Streetlights shimmer on the pavement\n    Midnight breathing soft and slow\n\n    [Chorus]\n    Stay with me until the morning\n    Let the city fade away\n\nYou can use:\n\n`[Verse]` · `[Chorus]` · `[Bridge]` · `[Outro]`\n\nFor better melody matching, keep the new lyrics reasonably close to the original phrasing and syllable count.\n\n## How the Cover Works\n\nThe workflow does not directly use the reference audio as YuE2 conditioning.\n\nInstead:\n\n    Reference Audio\n        ↓\n    SheetSage2\n        ↓\n    Melody ABC\n        ↓\n    YuE2 + Style + Lyrics\n        ↓\n    New Cover Audio\n\nSheetSage2 converts the source recording into a symbolic melody representation. YuE2 then uses that melody as the musical plan for the new cover.\n\n## Tips\n\n- Keep **Style** focused on the target sound, not the original sound.\n- Use **melody-only** planning for most cover tasks.\n- Changing the Style can create a very different arrangement while preserving the melody.\n- Lyrics can be changed, but similar phrasing and syllable counts usually fit the original melody better.\n- For a simple style-transfer test, keep the original lyrics and only change the Style.\n- For a stronger reinterpretation, change both the Style and Lyrics.\n\n## Learn More\n\n- [YuE2 Cover Guide](https://github.com/multimodal-art-projection/YuE/blob/main/docs/covers.md)\n- [YuE2 Music Skill](https://github.com/multimodal-art-projection/YuE/blob/main/skills/yue2-music/SKILL.md)\n- [Generation & Covers Reference](https://github.com/multimodal-art-projection/YuE/blob/main/skills/yue2-music/references/generation-and-covers.md)\n\n## Report Issue\n\nNote: Please update ComfyUI first ([guide](https://docs.comfy.org/installation/update_comfyui)) and prepare required models. Desktop/Cloud updates follow stable releases, so some nightly-supported models may not be available yet.\n\n- Cannot run / runtime errors: [ComfyUI/issues](https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI/issues)\n- UI / frontend issues: [ComfyUI_frontend/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI_frontend/issues)\n- Workflow issues: [workflow_templates/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/issues)\n"},"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":47,"type":"YuE2MemoryPreset","pos":[1442.7229370641603,314.4102180229809],"size":[388.38167936466937,118],"flags":{},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"vram","name":"vram","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"vram"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"memory_budget_gib","name":"memory_budget_gib","type":"INT","links":[98]},{"localized_name":"offload_ar","name":"offload_ar","type":"BOOLEAN","links":[99]},{"localized_name":"vae_decode","name":"vae_decode","type":"STRING","links":[]},{"localized_name":"vae_tile_frames","name":"vae_tile_frames","type":"INT",